### Description

The current `submit` function is `Promise` based, it would be great to have an alternative that works directly with `Observable`, similar to how the resource API provides both `resource` and `rxResource`.

It would also result in cleaner code when working with observables, avoiding the need for `async`/`await` or `Promise<void>`.

### Proposed solution

Introduce an `rxSubmit` function that accepts and handles an `Observable` as the return value.
```
protected handleSubmit(): void {
    rxSubmit(this.userForm, form => this.userApi.createUser(form().value()));
}
```

### Alternatives considered

Using `firstValueFrom` to convert an `Observable` into a `Promise`.

```
protected async handleSubmit(): Promise<void> {
    await submit(this.userForm, form => {
        const createUserRequest$ = this.userApi.createUser(form().value());
        return firstValueFrom(createUserRequest$);
    });
}
```

